  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Healthcare Access for Vulnerable Populations in Baalbeck El Hermel</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to this crisis, the IRC proposes to provide life-saving healthcare assistance through partnering with Baalbeck Social Health Center, a well-known Primary Health Care Center (PHCC) in Baalbeck district. Under this intervention, the IRC will support the PHCC in providing medical consultations covering mother and childcare, ante natal and post-natal care, sexual and reproductive health, communicable and non-communicable diseases, provision of mental health and psychosocial support services (MHPSS), coverage of diagnostic exams, provision of medications, immunization for children and malnutrition screening. Throughout these activities, the main focus will be on children under five, pregnant and lactating women, people with non-communicable diseases and mental health conditions. Services will take place at the PHCC and at the community level through mobile teams, ensuring that services will be accessible to everyone. Community based interventions will include health awareness, screenings for communicable diseases, non-communicable diseases, malnutrition, and mental health conditions. The IRC and its partner aim to target 4,000 beneficiaries, including vulnerable Lebanese and Syrian Refugees.</narrative>
  </description>
